# System rolling-log audit checklist

- [ ] Logging creates only the configured `system/logs/` local runtime directory.
- [ ] Repeated `get_logger()` calls do not duplicate handlers for the same logger.
- [ ] Rotation remains bounded at 1 MiB per file and 500 backups unless a current ruling changes it.
- [ ] Logs do not become a stable truth source and must not include secrets or hidden qualification data.
- [ ] Tests and audits that call this module isolate or clean their temporary runtime effects.
